      "execution": {
        "startingPosition": "Kneel tall with both lower legs held firmly by a partner, the hips and trunk neutral, and the arms reaching forward without touching the floor.",
        "movement": "Keep the hips and trunk aligned while lowering forward from the knees for three seconds through the range you can control.",
        "endpoint": "Stop at the furthest controlled position before the hips or trunk break alignment.",
        "returnPhase": "Actively flex both knees and pull the body back to tall kneeling over three seconds without pushing from the hands.",
        "controlledJoints": "Let knee extension occur only during the controlled lowering phase and create the return through knee flexion.",
        "supportAndPosture": "Keep the partner anchor secure and hold the hips, pelvis, and spine steady.",
        "disqualifyingCompensations": ["Touching down or pushing from the hands makes the repetition an assisted reset.", "Bending at the hips changes the reviewed Nordic fixture.", "Omitting the active return creates an eccentric-only repetition."]
